<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia's Sin Heng still suspended.</title>
<headline>Malaysia's Sin Heng still suspended.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poultry concern Sin Heng Chan (M) Bhd has been granted a further extension of its stock suspension until September 10, the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The shares last closed at 48.75 ringgit on July 19.</p>
<p>On July 25, the company said it was appealing to the Securities Commission to reconsider its decision on the company's proposed acquisition of gaming firm Stenworld Ltd. On that date, it also said it had asked the stock exchange for a continued suspension of its shares.</p>
<p>- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230 8911)</p>
